# Golden: voice-leading (D41) over a |C|G| change, ballad varA. The strings pad
# and the E.Piano second comp carry VoicingPolicy::kLead: across the change each
# voice re-octaves to the NEAREST register of the previous chord instead of
# jumping to the authored one. On C->G that is audible — the authored G triad
# would sit a fourth/fifth up (55/59/62), but kLead pulls it down to 43/47/50,
# the minimal move from the C voicing 48/52/55. Bass and the rising arpeggio
# (kChord1) stay kAsWritten.
key C major
port open out virt as synth
chord out synth:4
style load ballad
style route bass synth:2
style route chord1 synth:3
style route chord2 synth:6
style route pad synth:5
style section varA
seq new verse
seq add C 1bar
seq add G 1bar
seq loop on
seq play
transport start
advance 7680
quit
